.TH SINPI 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
sinpi, cospi, tanpi, asinpi, atanpi \- pi-argument trigonometric functions
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.B double sinpi(double x);
.B double cospi(double x);
.B double tanpi(double x);
.B double asinpi(double x);
.B double atanpi(double x);
.PP
.B float sinpif(float x);
.B float cospif(float x);
.B float tanpif(float x);
.B float asinpif(float x);
.B float atanpif(float x);
.PP
.B long double sinpil(long double x);
.B long double cospil(long double x);
.B long double tanpil(long double x);
.B long double asinpil(long double x);
.B long double atanpil(long double x);
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions compute the trigonometric functions with arguments expressed
in multiples of \fB\pi\fR radians. They are defined as:
.TP
.B sinpi(x)
Returns \fBsin(\fB\pi\fR x)\fR.
.TP
.B cospi(x)
Returns \fBcos(\fB\pi\fR x)\fR.
.TP
.B tanpi(x)
Returns \fBtan(\fB\pi\fR x)\fR.
.TP
.B asinpi(x)
Returns \fBasin(x)\fR / \fB\pi\fR. Equivalent to \fB1/\fR\fB\pi\fR times the
arc sine of \fBx\fR.
.TP
.B atanpi(x)
Returns \fBatan(x)\fR / \fB\pi\fR. Equivalent to \fB1/\fR\fB\pi\fR times the
arc tangent of \fBx\fR.
.PP
For integer values of \fBx\fR, the implementations exploit the mathematical
identities to compute exact results without floating-point transcendental
operations:
.RS
.TP
.B sinpi(\fIn\fR)
Returns exactly 0 for integer \fIn\fR.
.TP
.B cospi(\fIn\fR)
Returns exactly +1 or \-1 for integer \fIn\fR.
.TP
.B tanpi(\fIn\fR)
Returns exactly 0 for integer \fIn\fR.
.TP
.B asinpi(\fIn\fR)
Returns 0 for \fIn\fR = 0, +1/\fB\pi\fR or \-1/\fB\pi\fR for \fIn\fR = \fB\pm\fR1.
.TP
.B atanpi(\fIn\fR)
Returns 0 for \fIn\fR = 0, +1/4 or \-1/4 for \fIn\fR = \fB\pm\fR1.
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
All functions return the computed trigonometric value.
.PP
For \fBtanpi(x)\fR:
.RS
.TP
Returns \fBNaN\fR when \fBx\fR is a half-integer (e.g., 0.5, 1.5, \-0.5).
.TP
Returns \fB+\fR or \fB\-\fR infinity when \fBx\fR is infinity.
.TP
Returns \fBNaN\fR when \fBx\fR is \fBNaN\fR.
.RE
.PP
For \fBasinpi(x)\fR:
.RS
.TP
Returns \fBNaN\fR when |x| > 1 (domain error).
.TP
Returns \fBNaN\fR when x is \fBNaN\fR.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Evaluate the pi-argument trig functions at a half turn.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <math.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    double x = 0.5;

    printf("sinpi(%.1f) = %.6f\en", x, sinpi(x));
    printf("cospi(%.1f) = %.6f\en", x, cospi(x));
    printf("tanpi(%.1f) = %.6f\en", x, tanpi(x));
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
.SH STANDARDS
C23 (ISO/IEC 9899:2024), pi-argument trig functions (Clause 7.12.16).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sin (3),
.BR cos (3),
.BR tan (3),
.BR asin (3),
.BR math (7)
